# tithe4 - the DENSE face
#
# Three pixels wide is what puts FOUR stats in a CGA cell: the stat column
# is 24 pixels and the cell 20 rows, which at a 4x6 advance is six columns
# by three rows - HP on one, POWER on the next, and the two variable stats
# sharing the third. At 5x7 it is four by two and the fourth has nowhere to
# go. What three pixels CANNOT carry is an alphabet: M, N and W have one
# form each here and they are the only ones there are.
#
# 4x6 cell, 3x5 ink - the last column and the last row are the
# ADVANCE, so a run of glyphs never needs a gap put between them.
# Codes 1..7 are the stat ICONS: one glyph set and one renderer, so a
# number and the thing it is a number OF are drawn the same way.
#
# '#' IS BOTH THE INK AND THE COMMENT MARKER, so a reader must test
# for a PIXEL ROW before it tests for a comment - tools/os88font.py
# carries the same warning and this file's reader walked into it.

char 1   icon
#.#.
